{"type":"message","id":"d5387a03","parentId":"883c708f","timestamp":"2026-03-08T10:34:55.819Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_296b5a5946304094a717ea32","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Event Table Partitioning - Implementation Analysis\n\n**Date:** 2026-03-08  \n**Feature:** SQLite Event Table Partitioning  \n**Priority:** HIGH (unbounded table growth, query performance degradation)  \n**Impact:** 10-50x faster historical queries, automatic data lifecycle\n\n---\n\n## Problem Statement\n\n### Current Implementation\n```sql\n-- Single unbounded table\nCREATE TABLE agent_events (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source TEXT NOT NULL,\n  timestamp INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  data TEXT NOT NULL,\n  metadata TEXT DEFAULT '{}',\n  created_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch())\n)\n\n-- Indexes\nCREATE INDEX idx_agent_events_type ON agent_events(type, timestamp)\nCREATE INDEX idx_agent_events_source ON agent_events(source, timestamp)\n```\n\n### Issues\n1. **Unbounded Growth**: Table grows forever, no cleanup mechanism\n2. **Query Slowdown**: Historical queries get slower as table size increases\n3. **No Data Lifecycle**: No way to archive/delete old events\n4. **Single-Writer Bottleneck**: All writes to one table\n\n### Expected Data Volume\n- **Per day**: ~1000-5000 events (moderate usage)\n- **Per month**: ~30,000-150,000 events\n- **Per year**: ~365,000-1,800,000 events\n- **Query impact**: 100ms (1000 rows) → 10s (1M rows)\n\n---\n\n## Proposed Solution: Time-Based Partitioning\n\n### Design Principles\n1. **Monthly partitions**: Balance between file count and query performance\n2. **Automatic creation**: Create next month's partition before needed\n3. **Automatic cleanup**: Drop partitions older than retention period\n4. **Transparent queries**: Use UNION VIEW for backward compatibility\n\n### Partition Schema\n```sql\n-- Base template (not created directly)\n-- agent_events_YYYY_MM structure:\nCREATE TABLE agent_events_YYYY_MM (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  type TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source TEXT NOT NULL,\n  timestamp INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  data TEXT NOT NULL,\n  metadata TEXT DEFAULT '{}',\n  created_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch())\n);\n\n-- Per-partition indexes\nCREATE INDEX idx_events_YYYY_MM_type ON agent_events_YYYY_MM(type, timestamp);\nCREATE INDEX idx_events_YYYY_MM_source ON agent_events_YYYY_MM(source, timestamp);\nCREATE INDEX idx_events_YYYY_MM_time ON agent_events_YYYY_MM(timestamp);\n\n-- Unified view (backward compatibility)\nCREATE VIEW agent_events AS\n  SELECT * FROM agent_events_2026_01\n  UNION ALL SELECT * FROM agent_events_2026_02\n  UNION ALL SELECT * FROM agent_events_2026_03\n  -- ... dynamic based on available partitions\n;\n```\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n### 1. Partition Manager Class\n\n```typescript\n// src/infra/event-partition-manager.ts\n\nimport type { DatabaseSync } from \"node:sqlite\";\nimport { createSubsystemLogger } from \"../logging/subsystem.js\";\n\nconst log = createSubsystemLogger(\"event-partition\");\n\nexport type PartitionConfig = {\n  /** Months to keep (default: 12) */\n  retentionMonths: number;\n  /** Create partitions this many months ahead (default: 1) */\n  createAheadMonths: number;\n  /** Check interval for partition maintenance (default: 1 hour) */\n  maintenanceIntervalMs: number;\n};\n\nconst DEFAULT_CONFIG: PartitionConfig = {\n  retentionMonths: 12,\n  createAheadMonths: 1,\n  maintenanceIntervalMs: 3600000, // 1 hour\n};\n\nexport class EventPartitionManager {\n  private db: DatabaseSync;\n  private config: PartitionConfig;\n  private maintenanceTimer?: ReturnType<typeof setInterval>;\n  private currentPartitions: Set<string> = new Set();\n\n  constructor(db: DatabaseSync, config: Partial<PartitionConfig> = {}) {\n    this.db = db;\n    this.config = { ...DEFAULT_CONFIG, ...config };\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Initialize partition system\n   * - Create current month partition if not exists\n   * - Create next month partition\n   * - Build partition registry\n   * - Start maintenance timer\n   */\n  async initialize(): Promise<void> {\n    // Scan existing partitions\n    this.scanPartitions();\n\n    // Create current partition\n    const now = new Date();\n    await this.createPartitionForDate(now);\n\n    // Create next month partition\n    const nextMonth = new Date(now);\n    nextMonth.setMonth(nextMonth.getMonth() + 1);\n    await this.createPartitionForDate(nextMonth);\n\n    // Start maintenance\n    this.startMaintenance();\n\n    log.info(\n      `Event partitioning initialized (${this.currentPartitions.size} partitions, ` +\n        `retention: ${this.config.retentionMonths} months)`\n    );\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get partition name for a timestamp\n   */\n  getPartitionName(timestamp: number): string {\n    const date = new Date(timestamp);\n    const year = date.getFullYear();\n    const month = String(date.getMonth() + 1).padStart(2, \"0\");\n    return `agent_events_${year}_${month}`;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Create partition table for a given date\n   */\n  private async createPartitionForDate(date: Date): Promise<void> {\n    const partitionName = this.getPartitionName(date.getTime());\n\n    if (this.currentPartitions.has(partitionName)) {\n      return; // Already exists\n    }\n\n    try {\n      // Create partition table\n      this.db.prepare(`\n        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ${partitionName} (\n          id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n          type TEXT NOT NULL,\n          source TEXT NOT NULL,\n          timestamp INTEGER NOT NULL,\n          data TEXT NOT NULL,\n          metadata TEXT DEFAULT '{}',\n          created_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch())\n        )\n      `).run();\n\n      // Create indexes\n      this.db.prepare(`\n        CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_${partitionName}_type \n        ON ${partitionName}(type, timestamp)\n      `).run();\n\n      this.db.prepare(`\n        CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_${partitionName}_source \n        ON ${partitionName}(source, timestamp)\n      `).run();\n\n      this.db.prepare(`\n        CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_${partitionName}_time \n        ON ${partitionName}(timestamp)\n      `).run();\n\n      this.currentPartitions.add(partitionName);\n      log.info(`Created event partition: ${partitionName}`);\n    } catch (error) {\n      log.error(`Failed to create partition ${partitionName}:`, error);\n      throw error;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Scan database for existing partitions\n   */\n  private scanPartitions(): void {\n    try {\n      const tables = this.db\n        .prepare(\n          \"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table' AND name LIKE 'agent_events_%'\"\n        )\n        .all() as { name: string }[];\n\n      this.currentPartitions = new Set(tables.map((t) => t.name));\n      log.debug(`Found ${this.currentPartitions.size} existing partitions`);\n    } catch (error) {\n      log.error(\"Failed to scan partitions:\", error);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Run periodic maintenance:\n   * - Create future partitions\n   * - Drop old partitions\n   * - Rebuild view\n   */\n  private async runMaintenance(): Promise<void> {\n    log.debug(\"Running partition maintenance...\");\n\n    // Scan for new partitions (might have been created externally)\n    this.scanPartitions();\n\n    // Create partitions for next N months\n    const now = new Date();\n    for (let i = 0; i <= this.config.createAheadMonths; i++) {\n      const future = new Date(now);\n      future.setMonth(future.getMonth() + i);\n      await this.createPartitionForDate(future);\n    }\n\n    // Drop old partitions\n    const cutoff = new Date(now);\n    cutoff.setMonth(cutoff.getMonth() - this.config.retentionMonths);\n    await this.dropOldPartitions(cutoff);\n\n    // Rebuild unified view\n    this.rebuildView();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Drop partitions older than cutoff date\n   */\n  private async dropOldPartitions(cutoff: Date): Promise<void> {\n    const cutoffName = this.getPartitionName(cutoff.getTime());\n\n    for (const partitionName of this.currentPartitions) {\n      if (partitionName < cutoffName) {\n        try {\n          this.db.prepare(`DROP TABLE IF EXISTS ${partitionName}`).run();\n          this.currentPartitions.delete(partitionName);\n          log.info(`Dropped old partition: ${partitionName}`);\n        } catch (error) {\n          log.error(`Failed to drop partition ${partitionName}:`, error);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Rebuild unified view with all partitions\n   */\n  private rebuildView(): void {\n    try {\n      // Drop old view\n      this.db.prepare(\"DROP VIEW IF EXISTS agent_events\").run();\n\n      // Build UNION ALL query\n      const partitions = Array.from(this.currentPartitions).sort();\n      if (partitions.length === 0) {\n        log.warn(\"No partitions found, skipping view rebuild\");\n        return;\n      }\n\n      const unionQuery = partitions\n        .map((p) => `SELECT * FROM ${p}`)\n        .join(\"\\n  UNION ALL\\n  \");\n\n      this.db.prepare(`CREATE VIEW agent_events AS\\n  ${unionQuery}`).run();\n\n      log.debug(`Rebuilt view with ${partitions.length} partitions`);\n    } catch (error) {\n      log.error(\"Failed to rebuild view:\", error);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Start maintenance timer\n   */\n  private startMaintenance(): void {\n    this.maintenanceTimer = setInterval(\n      () => this.runMaintenance(),\n      this.config.maintenanceIntervalMs\n    );\n\n    // Don't prevent process exit\n    if (this.maintenanceTimer.unref) {\n      this.maintenanceTimer.unref();\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Stop maintenance and cleanup\n   */\n  async shutdown(): Promise<void> {\n    if (this.maintenanceTimer) {\n      clearInterval(this.maintenanceTimer);\n      this.maintenanceTimer = undefined;\n    }\n\n    log.info(\"Event partition manager shutdown\");\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get partition statistics\n   */\n  getStats() {\n    return {\n      partitionCount: this.currentPartitions.size,\n      partitions: Array.from(this.currentPartitions).sort(),\n      retentionMonths: this.config.retentionMonths,\n    };\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Manually trigger maintenance (for testing)\n   */\n  async triggerMaintenance(): Promise<void> {\n    await this.runMaintenance();\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Integration with Event Mesh\n\n```typescript\n// Modified src/agents/event-mesh.ts\n\nimport { EventPartitionManager } from \"../infra/event-partition-manager.js\";\n\nexport type EventMeshConfig = {\n  agentId: string;\n  db: DatabaseSync | null;\n  enablePersistence?: boolean;\n  maxListeners?: number;\n  // NEW: Partitioning config\n  partitioning?: {\n    enabled: boolean;\n    retentionMonths?: number;\n    createAheadMonths?: number;\n  };\n  // ... existing fields\n};\n\nexport class AgentEventMesh {\n  private partitionManager?: EventPartitionManager;\n\n  constructor(config: EventMeshConfig) {\n    // ... existing initialization ...\n\n    // Initialize partitioning if enabled\n    if (this.db && config.enablePersistence && config.partitioning?.enabled) {\n      this.partitionManager = new EventPartitionManager(this.db, {\n        retentionMonths: config.partitioning.retentionMonths,\n        createAheadMonths: config.partitioning.createAheadMonths,\n      });\n\n      // Initialize asynchronously (non-blocking)\n      this.partitionManager.initialize().catch((err) => {\n        log.warn(\"Failed to initialize partition manager:\", err);\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Persist event to database (with partition routing)\n   */\n  private persistEvent(event: AgentEvent): void {\n    if (!this.db) return;\n\n    try {\n      // Determine target partition\n      const partitionName = this.partitionManager\n        ? this.partitionManager.getPartitionName(event.timestamp)\n        : \"agent_events\"; // Fallback to legacy table\n\n      // Insert into partition\n      this.db\n        .prepare(\n          `INSERT INTO ${partitionName} \n           (id, type, source, timestamp, data, metadata)\n           VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)`\n        )\n        .run(\n          event.id,\n          event.type,\n          event.source,\n          event.timestamp,\n          JSON.stringify(event.data),\n          JSON.stringify(event.metadata || {})\n        );\n    } catch (error) {\n      const errorMsg = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n      log.error(`Failed to persist event: ${errorMsg}`);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Stop event mesh and cleanup\n   */\n  async stop(): Promise<void> {\n    if (this.partitionManager) {\n      await this.partitionManager.shutdown();\n    }\n    // ... existing cleanup ...\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get partition stats\n   */\n  getPartitionStats() {\n    return this.partitionManager?.getStats() ?? null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Migration Strategy\n\n```typescript\n// src/infra/event-partition-migration.ts\n\nimport type { DatabaseSync } from \"node:sqlite\";\nimport { createSubsystemLogger } from \"../logging/subsystem.js\";\n\nconst log = createSubsystemLogger(\"partition-migration\");\n\n/**\n * Migrate from single table to partitioned tables\n * \n * Steps:\n * 1. Create partition tables\n * 2. Copy data to appropriate partitions\n * 3. Drop old table\n * 4. Create unified view\n */\nexport async function migrateToPartitions(\n  db: DatabaseSync,\n  batchSize: number = 10000\n): Promise<void> {\n  log.info(\"Starting partition migration...\");\n\n  // Check if migration needed\n  const legacyTable = db\n    .prepare(\n      \"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table' AND name='agent_events'\"\n    )\n    .get();\n\n  if (!legacyTable) {\n    log.info(\"No legacy table found, migration not needed\");\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // Get event count\n  const count = db\n    .prepare(\"SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM agent_events\")\n    .get() as { count: number };\n\n  log.info(`Migrating ${count.count} events to partitions...`);\n\n  // Group events by month\n  const months = db\n    .prepare(\n      `SELECT \n        strftime('%Y-%m', timestamp, 'unixepoch') as month,\n        COUNT(*) as count,\n        MIN(timestamp) as start_time,\n        MAX(timestamp) as end_time\n       FROM agent_events\n       GROUP BY month\n       ORDER BY month`\n    )\n    .all() as { month: string; count: number; start_time: number; end_time: number }[];\n\n  log.info(`Found ${months.length} months of data`);\n\n  // Create partitions and migrate data\n  for (const monthData of months) {\n    const [year, month] = monthData.month.split(\"-\");\n    const partitionName = `agent_events_${year}_${month}`;\n\n    log.info(\n      `Migrating ${monthData.count} events to ${partitionName}...`\n    );\n\n    // Create partition\n    db.prepare(`\n      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ${partitionName} (\n        id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n        type TEXT NOT NULL,\n        source TEXT NOT NULL,\n        timestamp INTEGER NOT NULL,\n        data TEXT NOT NULL,\n        metadata TEXT DEFAULT '{}',\n        created_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch())\n      )\n    `).run();\n\n    // Create indexes\n    db.prepare(`\n      CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_${partitionName}_type \n      ON ${partitionName}(type, timestamp)\n    `).run();\n\n    db.prepare(`\n      CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_${partitionName}_source \n      ON ${partitionName}(source, timestamp)\n    `).run();\n\n    db.prepare(`\n      CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_${partitionName}_time \n      ON ${partitionName}(timestamp)\n    `).run();\n\n    // Copy data in batches\n    const startDate = new Date(monthData.start_time * 1000);\n    const endDate = new Date(monthData.end_time * 1000);\n    endDate.setMonth(endDate.getMonth() + 1);\n    endDate.setDate(0); // Last day of month\n\n    const startTs = Math.floor(startDate.getTime() / 1000);\n    const endTs = Math.floor(endDate.getTime() / 1000);\n\n    let migrated = 0;\n    while (migrated < monthData.count) {\n      const batch = db.prepare(`\n        INSERT INTO ${partitionName}\n        SELECT * FROM agent_events\n        WHERE timestamp >= ? AND timestamp <= ?\n        LIMIT ? OFFSET ?\n      `).run(startTs, endTs, batchSize, migrated);\n\n      migrated += batch.changes;\n\n      if (migrated < monthData.count) {\n        log.debug(`  Migrated ${migrated}/${monthData.count} events...`);\n      }\n    }\n\n    log.info(`✅ Migrated ${migrated} events to ${partitionName}`);\n  }\n\n  // Drop old table\n  log.warn(\"Dropping legacy agent_events table...\");\n  db.prepare(\"DROP TABLE agent_events\").run();\n\n  // Create unified view\n  const partitions = months\n    .map((m) => `agent_events_${m.month.replace(\"-\", \"_\")}`)\n    .sort();\n\n  const unionQuery = partitions\n    .map((p) => `SELECT * FROM ${p}`)\n    .join(\"\\n  UNION ALL\\n  \");\n\n  db.prepare(`CREATE VIEW agent_events AS\\n  ${unionQuery}`).run();\n\n  log.info(\"✅ Partition migration complete!\");\n  log.info(`Created ${partitions.length} partitions`);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Query Performance Impact\n\n### Before Partitioning\n```sql\n-- Query last month of events (1M total rows)\nSELECT * FROM agent_events \nWHERE timestamp >= 1706745600 \n  AND type = 'tool.execute'\nORDER BY timestamp DESC;\n\n-- Execution time: ~2000ms\n-- Rows scanned: 1,000,000\n-- Index usage: Partial (type, timestamp)\n```\n\n### After Partitioning\n```sql\n-- Query hits only 1 partition (50k rows)\nSELECT * FROM agent_events \nWHERE timestamp >= 1706745600 \n  AND type = 'tool.execute'\nORDER BY timestamp DESC;\n\n-- Execution time: ~40ms (50x faster)\n-- Rows scanned: 50,000 (in single partition)\n-- Index usage: Full (partition pruning + index)\n```\n\n### Performance Gains\n| Query Type | Before | After | Improvement |\n|------------|--------|-------|-------------|\n| Recent events (last month) | 2000ms | 40ms | **50x faster** |\n| Historical query (last year) | 15000ms | 500ms | **30x faster** |\n| Single event by ID | 50ms | 5ms | **10x faster** |\n| Delete old events | 5000ms | 5ms | **1000x faster** (DROP vs DELETE) |\n\n---\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n### 1. Partition Creation Failure\n```typescript\n// Retry with exponential backoff\nprivate async createPartitionWithRetry(date: Date, retries = 3): Promise<void> {\n  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {\n    try {\n      await this.createPartitionForDate(date);\n      return;\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (i === retries - 1) throw error;\n      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1000 * Math.pow(2, i)));\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Missing Partition Fallback\n```typescript\n// In persistEvent()\ntry {\n  // Try partition insert\n  this.db.prepare(`INSERT INTO ${partitionName} ...`).run(...);\n} catch (error) {\n  // Fallback to legacy table if partition doesn't exist\n  log.warn(`Partition ${partitionName} missing, falling back to legacy table`);\n  this.db.prepare(`INSERT INTO agent_events_legacy ...`).run(...);\n}\n```\n\n### 3. View Rebuild During Query\n```typescript\n// Use transaction to prevent race condition\nprivate rebuildView(): void {\n  this.db.transaction(() => {\n    this.db.prepare(\"DROP VIEW IF EXISTS agent_events\").run();\n    this.db.prepare(`CREATE VIEW agent_events AS ...`).run();\n  })();\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Clock Skew (future events)\n```typescript\n// Create partition for future events\nconst eventDate = new Date(event.timestamp);\nconst now = new Date();\n\nif (eventDate > now) {\n  // Ensure future partition exists\n  await this.createPartitionForDate(eventDate);\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Empty Months\n```typescript\n// Don't create partitions for months with no data\n// Only create when first event for that month arrives\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Tests\n```typescript\ndescribe('EventPartitionManager', () => {\n  it('should create partition for current month', async () => {\n    const manager = new EventPartitionManager(db);\n    await manager.initialize();\n    \n    const partition = manager.getPartitionName(Date.now());\n    expect(partition).toMatch(/agent_events_\\d{4}_\\d{2}/);\n  });\n\n  it('should drop partitions older than retention period', async () => {\n    const manager = new EventPartitionManager(db, { retentionMonths: 1 });\n    await manager.initialize();\n    await manager.triggerMaintenance();\n    \n    const stats = manager.getStats();\n    // Only current + next month should exist\n    expect(stats.partitionCount).toBeLessThanOrEqual(2);\n  });\n\n  it('should rebuild view after partition changes', async () => {\n    // Create 3 partitions\n    // Drop 1 old partition\n    // Check view has 2 partitions\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### Integration Tests\n```typescript\ndescribe('Event Mesh with Partitions', () => {\n  it('should route events to correct partition', async () => {\n    const mesh = new AgentEventMesh({\n      enablePersistence: true,\n      partitioning: { enabled: true }\n    });\n\n    // Emit event with old timestamp\n    const oldEvent = { timestamp: Date.now() - 90 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000 };\n    mesh.emit(oldEvent);\n\n    // Verify event in correct partition\n  });\n\n  it('should query across partitions via view', async () => {\n    // Insert events into 3 partitions\n    // Query via unified view\n    // Verify all 3 months returned\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### Performance Tests\n```typescript\nit('should insert events faster with partitioning', async () => {\n  // Benchmark: Insert 1000 events\n  // Partitioned: ~500ms\n  // Unpartitioned: ~2000ms\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Options\n\n```typescript\n// Default config\nconst defaultConfig = {\n  partitioning: {\n    enabled: true,\n    retentionMonths: 12,      // Keep 1 year\n    createAheadMonths: 1,     // Create next month early\n    maintenanceIntervalMs: 3600000  // Check every hour\n  }\n};\n\n// High-volume config\nconst highVolumeConfig = {\n  partitioning: {\n    enabled: true,\n    retentionMonths: 3,       // Aggressive cleanup\n    createAheadMonths: 2,     // Create 2 months ahead\n    maintenanceIntervalMs: 1800000  // Check every 30 min\n  }\n};\n\n// Long-term retention config\nconst archivalConfig = {\n  partitioning: {\n    enabled: true,\n    retentionMonths: 36,      // Keep 3 years\n    createAheadMonths: 1,\n    maintenanceIntervalMs: 7200000  // Check every 2 hours\n  }\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Checklist\n\n### Phase 1: Core Implementation ✅\n- [ ] Create `EventPartitionManager` class\n- [ ] Add partition creation logic\n- [ ] Add partition dropping logic\n- [ ] Add view rebuilding logic\n- [ ] Add maintenance timer\n\n### Phase 2: Integration ✅\n- [ ] Integrate with `AgentEventMesh`\n- [ ] Modify `persistEvent()` for partition routing\n- [ ] Add partition config to `EventMeshConfig`\n- [ ] Add shutdown hook for cleanup\n\n### Phase 3: Migration ✅\n- [ ] Create migration script\n- [ ] Add batch migration logic\n- [ ] Add rollback capability\n- [ ] Test with real data\n\n### Phase 4: Testing ✅\n- [ ] Unit tests for partition manager\n- [ ] Integration tests for event mesh\n- [ ] Performance benchmarks\n- [ ] Edge case tests\n\n### Phase 5: Deployment ✅\n- [ ] Run migration on existing database\n- [ ] Monitor partition creation\n- [ ] Monitor query performance\n- [ ] Adjust retention policy as needed\n\n---\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n\n### Risk 1: Migration Data Loss\n- **Mitigation**: Backup database before migration\n- **Mitigation**: Test on copy first\n- **Mitigation**: Keep legacy table until verified\n\n### Risk 2: Missing Partition on Write\n- **Mitigation**: Auto-create missing partitions\n- **Mitigation**: Fallback to legacy table\n- **Mitigation**: Log warnings for monitoring\n\n### Risk 3: View Rebuild During Query\n- **Mitigation**: Use transactions\n- **Mitigation**: Rebuild during low-traffic periods\n- **Mitigation**: Use CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW\n\n### Risk 4: Clock Skew (Future Events)\n- **Mitigation**: Create future partitions on demand\n- **Mitigation**: Limit how far ahead to create\n\n---\n\n## Expected Impact\n\n### Performance\n- ✅ **10-50x faster** historical queries\n- ✅ **1000x faster** data cleanup (DROP vs DELETE)\n- ✅ **Constant-time** inserts (partition size bounded)\n\n### Storage\n- ✅ **Automatic cleanup** of old data\n- ✅ **Predictable storage** usage (12 months bounded)\n- ✅ **Easier archival** (partition files can be backed up separately)\n\n### Operations\n- ✅ **Transparent** to existing queries (via view)\n- ✅ **No code changes** needed in event consumers\n- ✅ **Self-maintaining** (auto partition creation/dropping)\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. **Review this analysis** for any missing edge cases\n2. **Confirm configuration** (retention period, batch sizes)\n3. **Implement `EventPartitionManager`** class\n4. **Integrate with event mesh**\n5. **Create migration script**\n6. **Test on staging database**\n7. **Deploy to production** (with backup)\n\n---\n\n**Ready for implementation review** - Awaiting feedback and go-ahead.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772966095817}}
{"type":"message","id":"50e1043e","parentId":"d5387a03","timestamp":"2026-03-08T10:37:07.239Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me analyze this implementation plan in detail. I'll look for:\n\n1. Bugs or edge cases missed\n2. Migration strategy safety\n3. Performance concerns with view rebuilding\n4. TypeScript implementation improvements\n5. SQLite-specific gotchas\n\nLet me go through each section systematically:\n\n## 1. Bugs and Edge Cases Missed\n\n### Bug 1: View is not updateable in SQLite\nA major bug: **SQLite views with UNION ALL are NOT updateable!** You cannot INSERT into a view that's a UNION of multiple tables. The `agent_events` view will work for SELECT but NOT for INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE. This means the `persistEvent()` method cannot just insert into the view - it must route to the correct partition table directly.\n\nLooking at the code, `persistEvent()` does try to insert into the partition directly:\n```typescript\nconst partitionName = this.partitionManager\n  ? this.partitionManager.getPartitionName(event.timestamp)\n  : \"agent_events\"; // Fallback to legacy table\n```\n\nBut this has its own issue - what if `partitionManager` exists but the partition hasn't been created yet? There's a race condition between event arrival and partition creation.\n\n### Bug 2: Transaction syntax error\n```typescript\nthis.db.transaction(() => {\n  this.db.prepare(\"DROP VIEW IF EXISTS agent_events\").run();\n  this.db.prepare(`CREATE VIEW agent_events AS ...`).run();\n})();\n```\n\nThe `transaction()` method in `node:sqlite` doesn't take a callback like this. It returns a function that wraps SQL statements. The correct pattern is:\n```typescript\nconst txn = this.db.transaction(() => {\n  this.db.prepare(\"DROP VIEW IF EXISTS agent_events\").run();\n  this.db.prepare(`CREATE VIEW agent_events AS ...`).run();\n});\ntxn();\n```\n\n### Bug 3: Migration batch INSERT...SELECT with LIMIT/OFFSET\n```sql\nINSERT INTO ${partitionName}\nSELECT * FROM agent_events\nWHERE timestamp >= ? AND timestamp <= ?\nLIMIT ? OFFSET ?\n```\n\nThis is problematic for two reasons:\n1. Without ORDER BY, the OFFSET is non-deterministic - you might insert the same rows multiple times or miss rows\n2. This could be very slow with large OFFSET values\n\n### Bug 4: Partition name comparison for dropping\n```typescript\nif (partitionName < cutoffName) {\n```\n\nString comparison works for `agent_events_YYYY_MM` format because the format is zero-padded. This is actually correct, but relies on the specific naming format. A comment would help.\n\n### Bug 5: Date calculation in migration\n```typescript\nconst startDate = new Date(monthData.start_time * 1000);\nconst endDate = new Date(monthData.end_time * 1000);\nendDate.setMonth(endDate.getMonth() + 1);\nendDate.setDate(0); // Last day of month\n```\n\nThis is buggy. If `end_time` is say Jan 31, then `endDate.setMonth(endDate.getMonth() + 1)` could end up in March (because Feb 31 doesn't exist), and then `setDate(0)` would give a wrong date. The proper way is to calculate from the month string.\n\n### Bug 6: getPartitionName doesn't validate timestamp\n```typescript\ngetPartitionName(timestamp: number): string {\n  const date = new Date(timestamp);\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\nIf `timestamp` is in seconds instead of milliseconds (a common source of bugs), this will return 1970 partitions. Should validate the timestamp is reasonable.\n\n### Bug 7: async on synchronous SQLite operations\nAll the `async` methods don't actually need to be async since `node:sqlite` DatabaseSync is synchronous. This isn't a bug per se, but it's misleading.\n\n### Bug 8: Race condition between initialize() and persistEvent()\nThe `partitionManager.initialize()` is called asynchronously and non-blocking:\n```typescript\nthis.partitionManager.initialize().catch((err) => { ... });\n```\n\nBut `persistEvent()` might be called before initialization completes, leading to missing partition errors.\n\n### Bug 9: Maintenance timer can fire during initialization\n`startMaintenance()` is called inside `initialize()`, but if the maintenance interval is very short, the timer could fire before `initialize()` finishes setting up initial state.\n\n## 2. Migration Strategy Safety\n\n### Issue 1: No backup/verification step\nThe migration drops the old table immediately without verifying the migrated data. A safer approach:\n1. Rename old table to `agent_events_backup` instead of dropping\n2. Verify row counts match\n3. Only drop backup after a grace period\n\n### Issue 2: No rollback capability\nIf migration fails halfway, there's no way to rollback. The migration should either:\n- Be idempotent (safe to run multiple times)\n- Have proper transaction wrapping\n- Keep the original data until verified\n\n### Issue 3: BATCH migration logic is broken\nThe OFFSET-based batching has issues:\n1. No ORDER BY means non-deterministic results\n2. What if new rows are inserted during migration?\n3. OFFSET gets progressively slower\n\nBetter approach: Use a cursor or timestamp-based batching.\n\n## 3. Performance Concerns with View Rebuilding\n\n### Concern 1: View rebuild blocks queries\nSQLite has a global write lock. When rebuilding the view, all reads are blocked. For a large number of partitions, the view creation could take noticeable time.\n\n### Concern 2: View compilation overhead\nEvery time the view is rebuilt, SQLite needs to re-parse and compile it. For queries against the view, SQLite might not efficiently prune partitions since it's a UNION ALL view, not a real partitioned table.\n\n### Concern 3: UNION ALL query planning\nSQLite's query planner doesn't know about partition pruning. A query with `WHERE timestamp >= X` against the view will still be planned as scanning all UNION branches, even though many could be eliminated statically. The optimizer will short-circuit at runtime, but the query plan is more complex.\n\n### Concern 4: Maintenance during peak traffic\nThe maintenance runs on a fixed interval, which could coincide with peak traffic. Should consider:\n- Running during off-peak hours\n- Adding jitter to the timer\n- Checking query load before rebuilding\n\n## 4. TypeScript Implementation Improvements\n\n### Improvement 1: Type safety for partition names\n```typescript\n// Use branded type for partition names\ntype PartitionName = string & { readonly __brand: 'PartitionName' };\n\nfunction isValidPartitionName(name: string): name is PartitionName {\n  return /^agent_events_\\d{4}_\\d{2}$/.test(name);\n}\n```\n\n### Improvement 2: Better error handling\n```typescript\n// Use Result type for fallible operations\ntype Result<T, E = Error> = { ok: true; value: T } | { ok: false; error: E };\n\nasync createPartitionForDate(date: Date): Promise<Result<void, PartitionError>>\n```\n\n### Improvement 3: Dependency injection for testability\n```typescript\ninterface PartitionStorage {\n  createTable(name: string, schema: string): void;\n  dropTable(name: string): void;\n  getTableNames(prefix: string): string[];\n}\n```\n\n### Improvement 4: Use Readonly types for config\n```typescript\nexport type PartitionConfig = Readonly<{\n  retentionMonths: number;\n  createAheadMonths: number;\n  maintenanceIntervalMs: number;\n}>;\n```\n\n### Improvement 5: Add partition manager state enum\n```typescript\nenum ManagerState {\n  Uninitialized,\n  Initializing,\n  Running,\n  ShuttingDown,\n  Shutdown\n}\n```\n\n## 5. SQLite-Specific Gotchas\n\n### Gotcha 1: SQLITE_MAX_COMPOUND_SELECT\nSQLite has a limit on the number of terms in a compound SELECT (UNION). The default is 500. If you have more than 500 monthly partitions (~41 years), the view creation will fail. This is unlikely but worth documenting.\n\n### Gotcha 2: no AUTOINCREMENT on TEXT primary keys\nThe schema doesn't use AUTOINCREMENT (good), but the comment could note that INTEGER PRIMARY KEY would be more efficient if ID generation changes.\n\n### Gotcha 3: VACUUM after dropping tables\nDropping tables doesn't immediately free disk space in SQLite. After migration, a VACUUM should be run to reclaim space:\n```typescript\ndb.prepare(\"VACUUM\").run();\n```\n\n### Gotcha 4: WAL mode considerations\nIf the database uses WAL mode, dropping tables and creating views can interact with checkpoint behavior. Should ensure the database is checkpointed before migration.\n\n### Gotcha 5: Connection pooling issues\nIf using multiple connections, the view definition changes might not be immediately visible to all connections. The view schema is connection-specific in some scenarios.\n\n### Gotcha 6: DBSchema and sqlite_master race\nReading from sqlite_master and then acting on it without a transaction can have race conditions with other writers.\n\nLet me now prepare a comprehensive review document with specific code corrections.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"# Event Table Partitioning Implementation Review\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe implementation plan is well-structured and addresses the core problem, but there are **several critical bugs** and **significant safety concerns** with the migration strategy. The view-based approach has inherent limitations that need addressing.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Critical Bugs & Edge Cases\n\n### 🔴 CRITICAL: SQLite Views with UNION ALL Are NOT Updateable\n\nThe biggest issue: **You cannot INSERT into a UNION ALL view in SQLite.** The plan correctly routes inserts to partition tables directly, but this creates a race condition:\n\n```typescript\n// In persistEvent() - partition may not exist yet!\nconst partitionName = this.partitionManager\n  ? this.partitionManager.getPartitionName(event.timestamp)\n  : \"agent_events\";\n```\n\n**Problem**: If `partitionManager.initialize()` hasn't completed (it's non-blocking), the partition doesn't exist and the INSERT fails.\n\n**Fix**:\n```typescript\nprivate async ensurePartitionExists(timestamp: number): Promise<string> {\n  const partitionName = this.getPartitionName(timestamp);\n  \n  if (!this.currentPartitions.has(partitionName)) {\n    // Synchronously create if missing (fast path - IF NOT EXISTS)\n    await this.createPartitionForDate(new Date(timestamp));\n  }\n  \n  return partitionName;\n}\n\n// In persistEvent:\nconst partitionName = await this.partitionManager.ensurePartitionExists(event.timestamp);\n```\n\n### 🔴 CRITICAL: Migration Batch Logic is Broken\n\n```typescript\n// BROKEN: No ORDER BY, OFFSET is non-deterministic\nINSERT INTO ${partitionName}\nSELECT * FROM agent_events\nWHERE timestamp >= ? AND timestamp <= ?\nLIMIT ? OFFSET ?\n```\n\n**Problems**:\n1. Without `ORDER BY`, SQLite doesn't guarantee which rows `OFFSET` skips\n2. You might insert duplicates or miss rows\n3. OFFSET performance degrades linearly\n\n**Fix** - Use id-based cursor batching:\n```typescript\n// Better approach: Use id ranges\nlet lastId: string | null = null;\nlet migrated = 0;\n\nwhile (migrated < monthData.count) {\n  const batch = lastId\n    ? db.prepare(`\n        INSERT INTO ${partitionName}\n        SELECT * FROM agent_events\n        WHERE timestamp >= ? AND timestamp <= ? AND id > ?\n        ORDER BY id\n        LIMIT ?\n      `).all(startTs, endTs, lastId, batchSize)\n    : db.prepare(`\n        INSERT INTO ${partitionName}\n        SELECT * FROM agent_events\n        WHERE timestamp >= ? AND timestamp <= ?\n        ORDER BY id\n        LIMIT ?\n      `).all(startTs, endTs, batchSize);\n\n  if (batch.length === 0) break;\n  \n  // Get last inserted id for next batch\n  const lastRow = db.prepare(`\n    SELECT id FROM ${partitionName} \n    WHERE timestamp >= ? AND timestamp <= ?\n    ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1\n  `).get(startTs, endTs) as { id: string } | undefined;\n  \n  lastId = lastRow?.id ?? null;\n  migrated += batch.length;\n}\n```\n\n### 🔴 CRITICAL: Transaction Syntax is Wrong\n\n```typescript\n// WRONG: node:sqlite transaction doesn't work like this\nthis.db.transaction(() => {\n  this.db.prepare(\"DROP VIEW IF EXISTS agent_events\").run();\n  this.db.prepare(`CREATE VIEW agent_events AS ...`).run();\n})();\n```\n\n**Fix**:\n```typescript\n// CORRECT: transaction() returns a wrapped function\nconst rebuildViewTxn = this.db.transaction(() => {\n  this.db.prepare(\"DROP VIEW IF EXISTS agent_events\").run();\n  this.db.prepare(`CREATE VIEW agent_events AS ...`).run();\n});\nrebuildViewTxn();\n```\n\n### 🟡 Date Calculation Bug in Migration\n\n```typescript\n// BUGGY: setMonth on Jan 31 could jump to March\nconst endDate = new Date(monthData.end_time * 1000);\nendDate.setMonth(endDate.getMonth() + 1);\nendDate.setDate(0);\n```\n\n**Example**: If `end_time` is Jan 31, `setMonth(1)` tries Feb 31 → auto-corrects to Mar 3 → `setDate(0)` gives Feb 28/29, not the intended Feb 28/29.\n\n**Fix** - Calculate from month string directly:\n```typescript\nconst [year, month] = monthData.month.split(\"-\");\nconst startTs = Math.floor(new Date(parseInt(year), parseInt(month) - 1, 1).getTime() / 1000);\n// Last second of month\nconst endTs = Math.floor(new Date(parseInt(year), parseInt(month), 0, 23, 59, 59).getTime() / 1000);\n```\n\n### 🟡 Race Condition: `persistEvent` Before Initialization\n\n```typescript\n// initialize() is non-blocking\nthis.partitionManager.initialize().catch((err) => { ... });\n\n// But persistEvent might be called immediately\n```\n\n**Fix** - Add initialization guard:\n```typescript\nexport class EventPartitionManager {\n  private initPromise?: Promise<void>;\n  private state: 'uninitialized' | 'initializing' | 'ready' = 'uninitialized';\n\n  async initialize(): Promise<void> {\n    if (this.state !== 'uninitialized') {\n      return this.initPromise;\n    }\n    \n    this.state = 'initializing';\n    this.initPromise = this.doInitialize();\n    await this.initPromise;\n    this.state = 'ready';\n  }\n\n  async ensureReady(): Promise<void> {\n    if (this.state !== 'ready') {\n      await this.initialize();\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 🟡 Timestamp Validation Missing\n\n```typescript\ngetPartitionName(timestamp: number): string {\n  const date = new Date(timestamp);\n  // What if timestamp is in seconds, not milliseconds?\n}\n```\n\n**Fix**:\n```typescript\ngetPartitionName(timestamp: number): string {\n  // Detect if timestamp is in seconds (before year 2001 in ms = before 1973 in s)\n  const adjustedTs = timestamp < 10000000000 ? timestamp * 1000 : timestamp;\n  \n  // Sanity check: must be after 2020 and before 2100\n  if (adjustedTs < 1577836800000 || adjustedTs > 4102444800000) {\n    throw new Error(`Invalid timestamp: ${timestamp} (adjusted: ${adjustedTs})`);\n  }\n  \n  const date = new Date(adjustedTs);\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Migration Strategy Safety Issues\n\n### 🔴 CRITICAL: No Verification Before Drop\n\n```typescript\n// DANGEROUS: Immediately drops source table\nlog.warn(\"Dropping legacy agent_events table...\");\ndb.prepare(\"DROP TABLE agent_events\").run();\n```\n\n**Fix** - Keep backup and verify:\n```typescript\nexport async function migrateToPartitions(db: DatabaseSync, options: {\n  batchSize?: number;\n  keepBackup?: boolean;\n  verifyBeforeDrop?: boolean;\n} = {}): Promise<void> {\n  const { batchSize = 10000, keepBackup = true, verifyBeforeDrop = true } = options;\n\n  // ... migration logic ...\n\n  // Get pre-migration count\n  const sourceCount = db.prepare(\"SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM agent_events\").get() as { count: number };\n  \n  // Get total migrated count\n  let migratedCount = 0;\n  for (const partition of partitions) {\n    const pCount = db.prepare(`SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM ${partition}`).get() as { count: number };\n    migratedCount += pCount.count;\n  }\n\n  // Verify counts match\n  if (verifyBeforeDrop && migratedCount !== sourceCount.count) {\n    throw new Error(\n      `Migration verification failed: source=${sourceCount.count}, migrated=${migratedCount}`\n    );\n  }\n\n  if (keepBackup) {\n    // Rename instead of drop\n    db.prepare(\"ALTER TABLE agent_events RENAME TO agent_events_pre_migration_backup\").run();\n    log.info(\"Renamed legacy table to agent_events_pre_migration_backup\");\n  } else {\n    db.prepare(\"DROP TABLE agent_events\").run();\n  }\n\n  // Post-migration: reclaim space\n  db.prepare(\"PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE)\").run();\n}\n```\n\n### 🔴 CRITICAL: No Rollback Capability\n\n**Fix** - Add rollback function:\n```typescript\nexport function rollbackMigration(db: DatabaseSync): void {\n  // Drop all partitions\n  const tables = db\n    .prepare(\"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table' AND name LIKE 'agent_events_%'\")\n    .all() as { name: string }[];\n\n  for (const t of tables) {\n    db.prepare(`DROP TABLE IF EXISTS ${t.name}`).run();\n  }\n\n  // Drop view\n  db.prepare(\"DROP VIEW IF EXISTS agent_events\").run();\n\n  // Restore backup if exists\n  const backup = db\n    .prepare(\"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table' AND name='agent_events_pre_migration_backup'\")\n    .get();\n\n  if (backup) {\n    db.prepare(\"ALTER TABLE agent_events_pre_migration_backup RENAME TO agent_events\").run();\n  }\n\n  log.info(\"Migration rolled back successfully\");\n}\n```\n\n### 🟡 Missing VACUUM After Drop\n\nDropping tables doesn't immediately free space in SQLite.\n\n**Fix**:\n```typescript\n// After dropping legacy table\nlog.info(\"Running VACUUM to reclaim disk space...\");\ndb.prepare(\"VACUUM\").run();\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Performance Concerns with View Rebuilding\n\n### 🟡 View Rebuild Blocks All Queries\n\nSQLite has a global write lock. During view rebuild, **all reads are blocked**.\n\n**Mitigation**:\n```typescript\nprivate rebuildView(): void {\n  const startTime = Date.now();\n  \n  // Use IMMEDIATE transaction to reduce lock contention\n  const txn = this.db.transaction(() => {\n    this.db.prepare(\"DROP VIEW IF EXISTS agent_events\").run();\n    // ... create new view ...\n  });\n  txn();\n  \n  const duration = Date.now() - startTime;\n  if (duration > 100) {\n    log.warn(`View rebuild took ${duration}ms - consider running during off-peak`);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 🟡 No Partition Pruning in Query Planning\n\nSQLite doesn't do partition pruning at query planning time for UNION ALL views. A query with `WHERE timestamp >= X` will have its query plan include all UNION branches.\n\n**Mitigation** - Query partitions directly when possible:\n```typescript\n// For time-range queries, query specific partition instead of view\nfunction queryEventsByTimeRange(startTs: number, endTs: number): AgentEvent[] {\n  const partitions = this.getPartitionsForTimeRange(startTs, endTs);\n  \n  const results: AgentEvent[] = [];\n  for (const partition of partitions) {\n    const rows = this.db.prepare(`\n      SELECT * FROM ${partition}\n      WHERE timestamp >= ? AND timestamp <= ?\n    `).all(startTs, endTs);\n    results.push(...rows);\n  }\n  \n  return results.sort((a, b) => a.timestamp - b.timestamp);\n}\n\nprivate getPartitionsForTimeRange(startTs: number, endTs: number): string[] {\n  return Array.from(this.currentPartitions).filter(p => {\n    const [year, month] = p.replace('agent_events_', '').split('_');\n    const partStart = new Date(parseInt(year), parseInt(month) - 1, 1).getTime() / 1000;\n    const partEnd = new Date(parseInt(year), parseInt(month), 0, 23, 59, 59).getTime() / 1000;\n    return partEnd >= startTs && partStart <= endTs;\n  });\n}\n```\n\n### 🟡 Maintenance During Peak Traffic\n\n**Fix** - Add adaptive scheduling:\n```typescript\nprivate shouldRunMaintenance(): boolean {\n  const hour = new Date().getHours();\n  // Avoid 9am-6pm for maintenance (configurable)\n  const offPeakHours = this.config.offPeakHours ?? { start: 22, end: 6 };\n  \n  if (hour >= offPeakHours.start || hour < offPeakHours.end) {\n    return true;\n  }\n  \n  log.debug(\"Skipping maintenance during peak hours\");\n  return false;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. TypeScript Implementation Improvements\n\n### Use Branded Types for Partition Names\n\n```typescript\ndeclare const PartitionNameBrand: unique symbol;\ntype PartitionName = string & { readonly [PartitionNameBrand]: true };\n\nfunction parsePartitionName(name: string): PartitionName | null {\n  const match = name.match(/^agent_events_(\\d{4})_(\\d{2})$/);\n  if (!match) return null;\n  return name as PartitionName;\n}\n\nfunction createPartitionName(year: number, month: number): PartitionName {\n  return `agent_events_${year}_${String(month).padStart(2, '0')}` as PartitionName;\n}\n```\n\n### Use Readonly Config and State Machine\n\n```typescript\ntype ManagerState = 'uninitialized' | 'initializing' | 'running' | 'shutting_down' | 'shutdown';\n\ntype PartitionConfig = Readonly<{\n  retentionMonths: number;\n  createAheadMonths: number;\n  maintenanceIntervalMs: number;\n  offPeakHours?: { start: number; end: number };\n}>;\n\nexport class EventPartitionManager {\n  private state: ManagerState = 'uninitialized';\n  private readonly config: PartitionConfig;\n  \n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n### Result Type for Fallible Operations\n\n```typescript\ntype Result<T, E = Error> = \n  | { ok: true; value: T }\n  | { ok: false; error: E };\n\ntype PartitionError = \n  | { type: 'invalid_timestamp'; timestamp: number }\n  | { type: 'create_failed'; partition: string; cause: Error }\n  | { type: 'not_initialized' };\n\nasync createPartitionForDate(date: Date): Promise<Result<void, PartitionError>> {\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n### Remove Async from Synchronous Operations\n\n```typescript\n// node:sqlite DatabaseSync is synchronous - no need for async\nprivate createPartitionForDate(date: Date): void {  // Not async!\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. SQLite-Specific Gotchas\n\n### 🔴 SQLITE_MAX_COMPOUND_SELECT Limit\n\nDefault limit is **500 UNION terms**. With monthly partitions, this means ~41 years before hitting the limit.\n\n**Mitigation** - Document and add guard:\n```typescript\nprivate rebuildView(): void {\n  if (this.currentPartitions.size > 400) {\n    log.error(`Too many partitions (${this.currentPartitions.size}) - approaching SQLITE_MAX_COMPOUND_SELECT limit`);\n    // Consider archiving old partitions instead\n  }\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n### 🟡 WAL Mode Checkpoint Before Migration\n\n```typescript\nexport async function migrateToPartitions(db: DatabaseSync): Promise<void> {\n  // Checkpoint WAL to ensure consistent state\n  db.prepare(\"PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE)\").run();\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n### 🟡 Schema Version Tracking\n\n```typescript\n// Add migration metadata table\ndb.prepare(`\n  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS _partition_schema (\n    version INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n    migrated_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch()),\n    config_json TEXT\n  )\n`).run();\n\n// Track migration\ndb.prepare(`\n  INSERT INTO _partition_schema (version, config_json)\n  VALUES (1, ?)\n`).run(JSON.stringify({ retentionMonths: 12 }));\n```\n\n### 🟡 Thread Safety with Shared Connections\n\nIf the database connection is shared across threads (worker threads), the in-memory `currentPartitions` set could become stale.\n\n**Mitigation**:\n```typescript\nprivate scanPartitions(): void {\n  // Always scan fresh from DB\n  const tables = this.db\n    .prepare(\"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table' AND name LIKE 'agent_events_%'\")\n    .all() as { name: string }[];\n\n  this.currentPartitions = new Set(tables.map(t => t.name));\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Required Fixes\n\n| Priority | Issue | Fix Required |\n|----------|-------|--------------|\n| 🔴 CRITICAL | Race condition in persistEvent | Add initialization guard, ensure partition exists before insert |\n| 🔴 CRITICAL | Migration batch logic broken | Use id-based cursor instead of OFFSET |\n| 🔴 CRITICAL | Transaction syntax wrong | Fix transaction() usage |\n| 🔴 CRITICAL | No verification before drop | Keep backup, verify counts |\n| 🔴 CRITICAL | No rollback capability | Add rollback function |\n| 🟡 HIGH | Date calculation bug | Calculate from month string |\n| 🟡 HIGH | View rebuild blocks queries | Use IMMEDIATE transaction, off-peak scheduling |\n| 🟡 MEDIUM | Timestamp validation missing | Add sanity check |\n| 🟡 MEDIUM | Missing VACUUM after migration | Add VACUUM call |\n| 🟢 LOW | SQLite UNION limit | Add guard for >400 partitions |\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Implementation Order\n\n1. **Fix critical bugs** (race condition, batch logic, transaction syntax)\n2. **Add safety mechanisms** (backup, verification, rollback)\n3. **Fix edge cases** (date calculation, timestamp validation)\n4. **Add performance mitigations** (partition-aware queries, off-peak maintenance)\n5. **Polish TypeScript** (branded types, state machine, result types)"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zhipu","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":5729,"output":5533,"cacheRead":13952,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25214,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1772966095819}}
